4. Main Results

Fix the number of agents n, the combination size k \ge 2, the synergy exponent \alpha > 0 satisfying \alpha(k-1) > 1 (so that the idea process is inherently explosive in a large enough component), the productivity P, the death rate \delta, the signal noise \sigma^2, and the learning rate \eta. Consider the limit n \to \infty while scaling p = p(n) and, consequently, \rho = p/\gamma.

Theorem 1 (Percolation–Discovery Thresholds).
Let \rho_c^- = 1/n. There exists a sequence \rho_c^+(n) > \rho_c^-(n) such that, under the mean‑field assumptions of Section 2, the following hold with probability tending to 1 as n \to \infty:

1. (Stagnation) If \rho < (1-\varepsilon)\rho_c^-, then \limsup_{t\to\infty} X(t) < \infty almost surely, the exploration set eventually becomes empty, and the belief vector does not converge to \theta.
2. (Discovery) If (1+\varepsilon)\rho_c^- < \rho < (1-\varepsilon)\rho_c^+, then a giant component forms in the cumulative exploration graph, X(t) \to \infty in finite expected time, and b(t) \to \theta \mathbf{1} in finite expected time.
3. (False lock‑in) If \rho > (1+\varepsilon)\rho_c^+, then b(t) converges to a consensus \hat b \mathbf{1} with \hat b \neq \theta with probability bounded away from zero, while X(t) remains stochastically bounded.

Conjectured scaling of the upper threshold.
Numerical and heuristic arguments (see Section 5.5) suggest that

\rho_c^+(n) = \frac{C \log n}{n} \bigl(1 + o(1)\bigr),

where C depends on k, \alpha, P, \delta, \eta, \sigma^2. This scaling coincides with the connectivity threshold of the cumulative exploration graph over the consensus time scale, and it recovers the classical Zollman window (1/n, \log n / n).

Theorem 2 (Entropy–Explosion Duality).
Let H(t) be the Shannon entropy of the empirical belief distribution at time t. Under the mean‑field coupling, at the upper threshold \rho = \rho_c^+ the expected rate of entropy decay balances the expected exponential growth rate of the idea pool:

\mathbb{E}\!\left[ \frac{dH}{dt} \right]_{\rho_c^+} = -\,\alpha(k-1)\; \mathbb{E}\!\left[ \frac{d}{dt}\log X(t) \right]_{\rho_c^+}. \tag{6}

Equivalently, the relaxation rate \gamma and the Malthusian growth rate r(X) of the idea process satisfy \gamma = r(X) at the threshold, where X is the characteristic size of the idea pool at the onset of explosion.

Remark. The duality is a consequence of the fact that the Shannon entropy of the belief distribution decays as -\gamma H near consensus, while the combinatorial explosion drives \log X with a growth rate proportional to X^{\alpha k -1}. The balance condition (6) picks out the critical effective connectivity.

